# L §5.14.1 bal(x, d) row: "For d on its day, a plain bal(x, d) would read the decision's own result, a cycle; for d
# after it, the decision's future. Both are refused: LOAD-CYCLE where load sees the day".  draw's day is d and its
# amount reads bal(konto, d): load sees the decision's own day.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-01-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2020-01-01..
place kredyt: accounts PLN lives 2020-01-01..

move draw[d in days]: transfers
  on d
  at d
  reads konto
  leg cash from kredyt to konto amount max(0 PLN, -bal(konto, d))

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[kredyt] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start

ask q: bal(konto, 2026-01-31)
=== expect
refused: LOAD-CYCLE ...
